# Repo Context — Chess SLM Benchmark ("something new")

Last updated: 2026-08-12 (commit `213c9e2`, branch `main`)

This file is the entry point for anyone (human or agent) inheriting this
repository: what the project is, everything that has been done so far, where
things stand right now, and the most recent changes.

---

## 1. What this project is

**Objective** (full statement: `docs/objective.md`, `README.md`): benchmark
Gemma 4 on chess and fine-tune it to play chess **better than DeepSeek V4
Flash using only natural-language reasoning** — no external search, no engine
at inference time.

**Thesis (current form):** small language models (SLMs) acquire stronger
reasoning by learning to reason in the compressed, telegraphic **"lucid /
caveman" style** that RL-post-trained frontier models natively use, compared
with standard verbose natural-language chain-of-thought. Chess (MATE
move-selection) is the cheap, verifiable testbed. Efficiency metric:
**tokens-per-correct**, not accuracy alone.

**Target venue:** Efficient and On-Device AI Agents Workshop @ NeurIPS 2026
(Sydney). Compute: Kaggle free T4 + opencode-go gateway API. Paper draft
lives in `paper/main.tex`.

**Key anchors:**
- MATE benchmark (Wang et al., NAACL 2025, arXiv:2411.06655) — position-level
  2-candidate move selection; authors' fine-tuned LLaMA-3-8B zero-shot:
  63.5% (N), 89.7% (S), 94.6% (T), 95.2% (ST).
- DeepSeek-R1 (arXiv:2501.12948) — the lucid-style teacher line + distillation
  recipe.
- cavegemma (GitHub, HF record `hf-cavegemma` in `.rstack/lit-review.jsonl`) —
  QLoRA recipe for teaching gemma to speak caveman-mode natively.

---

## 2. Research plan (locked pipeline)

The staged plan (committed in `idea.md` / `refined-idea.md`, locked in commit
`69b2483` "plan: lock the lucid-reasoning chess SLM pipeline"):

- **B** — baseline labels-only SFT (cheap baseline arm)
- **A1** — "caveman gemma": teach gemma-4-E2B the compressed reasoning style
  (cavegemma recipe: synthesize lucid rewrites → QLoRA SFT)
- **A2** — MATE lucid-traces: distill deepseek-v4-flash lucid reasoning traces
  on MATE positions into gemma (trace+answer vs answer-only comparison =
  A-vs-B design)
- **Refined idea** (`refined-idea.md`): a **phase-segregated** (opening /
  middlegame / endgame), engine-verified trace dataset + a phase-stratified
  benchmark released from the same pipeline — the primary paper contribution
  (novelty assessment in `novelty-assessment.md`, score 7/10).

---

## 3. Work done so far, in detail

### 3.1 Phase 1 — representation sensitivity study (completed)
- Measured representation sensitivity on standard-chess mate-in-1: **FEN 5/5,
  grid 3/5, list 3/5, bitboard 0/5** (bitboard produced illegal moves).
- Decision recorded: the study runs the **FEN representation only** — chess
  capability, not format adaptation. Full report: `docs/phase1-results.md`,
  raw data in `docs/phase1/` (deleted from repo in the Aug-2026 cleanup, see
  §6; report doc retained).

### 3.2 Evaluation harness + task sets (complete)
- Task sets under `data/positions/` with oracles and full lichess metadata:
  - `mate1-lichess.json`, `mate2-lichess.json` (250 each; lichess puzzle DB,
    CC0, engine-verified)
  - `bestmove-8x8.json` (120; lichess eval DB, Stockfish PV ground truth)
  - `mate-selection-test{-noexplain,-tactic,-both,strategy}.json` — the MATE
    4-subset × 1000-position campaign sets (build: `scripts/build_mate_evals.py`,
    protocol identical to the MATE authors: testset, FEN-dedupe, SEED 2026).
- Strict extraction + oracle scoring via python-chess (`src/benchmarks/games/`
  prompts/tasks). Honesty guarantees: no fallback answers, no fabricated
  content, gateway errors never scored as model output (documented in README).
- Regression gate: `scripts/test_engine.py` (dataset consistency + extraction
  regressions; the CI-style gate for this repo).

### 3.3 MATE 1000-position campaign (in progress)
Replicating the MATE authors' Table 1: 4 subsets × 1000 positions × {deepseek,
gemma}. Current state (README matrix):

| arm | strategy | noexplain | tactic | both |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| deepseek-v4-flash, thinking | **85.8%** (858/1000) ✓ | ran | ran | ran |
| gemma4-e2b, thinking, 32768 budget | **61.1%** (611/1000) ✓ | ran | ran | ran |
| gemma4-e2b MATE-LoRA fine-tune | — | — | — | — (next) |

- Deployment: 5 parallel CPU Kaggle kernels per subset for deepseek; GPU
  kernels (T4/P100) for gemma; a Kaggle-hosted **campaign watcher** auto-pushes
  waves; live state published to `monitor/` and `chess-bench-live.pages.dev`.
- Raw teacher samples for the strategy subset: 60 MB file — **mirrored to
  Hugging Face** (see §5) because it exceeds GitHub's 50 MB warning threshold.
- Results archive infra: `src/hf_push.py` publishes every completed cell
  (report.json + samples.jsonl + summary.json + index.json) to
  `vedangfake/chess-bench-results` (HF dataset).
- Deliberately NOT replicated: 3-candidate experiment, explanation generation,
  difficulty audit, few-shot (documented in README).

### 3.4 Self-play full-game trace distillation (designed + scaffolding done)
- `scripts/play_selfplay.py` — one deepseek-vs-deepseek full game:
  legality-enforced loop (python-chess), unbounded thinking, per-move live
  push, checkpoint resume.
- `scripts/run_selfplay_campaign.py` — parallel games (one API key per worker),
  live tournament index → `monitor/games/state.json`, HF resume for Kaggle
  restarts.
- `notebooks/build_selfplay_kernel_notebook.py` + `push_selfplay/` kernels.
- Design decisions (README §"The plan"): legality + opening-diversity (pool A
  seeded plies, pool B master-book middlegames), per-move Stockfish ±100cp
  soundness filter (both players, kills winner-bias), lucid/caveman trace
  compression pass ≤4k tokens per kept move (cavegemma 2-step recipe).
- **Status: not yet run at scale** — pilot pending (compute/API budget).

### 3.5 MATE-LoRA arm (data + training scaffolding complete)
- `data/positions/mate-lora/{train,eval}.jsonl` — **200k train / 5k eval**
  chat pairs from MATE noexplain train (~1.42M rows), FEN-deduped, test-set
  FENs excluded (contamination hygiene, seed 42). Prompt is byte-identical to
  the eval prompt (candidates + trailing space) so training matches scoring.
  Build: `scripts/build_mate_lora_data.py`.
- `scripts/train_mate_lora.py` — QLoRA SFT (unsloth-style, LoRA on E2B),
  args for smoke runs. `notebooks/build_mate_lora_kernel_notebook.py` +
  `push_gemma_*` kernels (noexplain/both/tactic + aggregator) built for
  Kaggle T4.
- **Status: not yet trained** (next on the GPU budget).

### 3.6 Phase-segregated dataset + benchmark (refined idea, built)
- `scripts/build_phase_dataset.py` — deterministic phase classifier (published
  artifact): opening = ply ≤ 12, endgame = non-king material ≤ threshold,
  else middlegame; samples per phase from MATE train with metadata schema.
- `data/positions/phase-train/strategy.positions.jsonl` + phase-manifest —
  generated phase pools.
- `scripts/build_phase_benchmark.py` — stratified holdout:
  `data/positions/phase-benchmark/benchmark.jsonl` (300/phase target,
  FEN-deduped vs training traces and MATE test sets, Stockfish ground truth).
- This is the primary paper contribution; novelty assessed 7/10
  (`novelty-assessment.md`).

### 3.7 "Caveman gemma" style teaching (literature grounded; next milestone)
- **Literature review on compressed/lucid reasoning — 26 new papers** appended
  to `.rstack/lit-review.jsonl` (now 40 records) and consolidated in
  `lit-review-lucid.md` (2026-08-12). Five approach families: prompting (Chain
  of Draft 2502.18600, Concise CoT 2401.05618), RL rewards (GFPO 2508.09726,
  shaping 2510.09535, theory 2504.05185), distillation/SFT (LS-Mixture SFT
  2505.03469, difficulty-aware pruning 2505.19716, self-training 2502.20122),
  latent reasoning (2311.01460, 2509.25239), adaptive compute (2505.11274,
  2601.02972). Two hard caveats: report accuracy AND tokens jointly; measure
  tokens on the deployed quantized model (2606.25519).
- Key thesis-supporting finding: **content, not length, drives CoT accuracy**
  (arXiv:2606.30128) — verbose traces buy nothing extra; lucid is not lossy.

### 3.8 Live dashboard + arena (built, deployed)
- `frontend/` — Cloudflare Pages dashboard `chess-bench-live.pages.dev`
  (index.html + styles.css + games.html/games.js self-play arena: live board
  + both sides' thinking).
- `worker/worker.js` — Cloudflare Worker proxy (fresh GitHub contents feed;
  `/games` routes).
- `monitor/` — aggregators + live state (gitignored; pushed to the
  `Vedang-P/chess-bench-live` repo by `scripts/aggregate_live_state.py`).

### 3.9 Retired work (deleted 2026-08-12, kept in git history)
- `chessreasoner` — a custom transformer + tokenizer + tier-1 generator
  (custom architecture experiment, commits `ecb9482`→`6aa6fba`); retired after
  adversarial testing; code + its 3D architecture site (`site/`) and
  `docs/architecture.md` removed.
- Phase-1 raw reports, old Kaggle notebooks, suite/config scaffolding —
  purged (`5129158` and the Aug-2026 cleanup). History preserves all of it.

